Patron's scoping of the rule.

Recorded against this opus, not waived
--------------------------------------
This opus's own twelve behaviours have no per-behaviour log in
studio/ci/reds/W-021/. Builder-b recorded a genuine red — a real failing run
of the full twelve-behaviour test file with the implementation moved out of
the tree, ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND, exit 1, captured before the implementation
existed — but recorded it outside the officina, because the store it would
have written to did not exist on master at the time.

The root cause is a cascade-ordering failure, not a builder's: the brief
required W-020 to land `bisellium red` on master as its first commit
precisely so that builder-b could record into the store, and the harness ran
both builders in parallel worktrees off one base, so that commit never
existed for builder-b to use. W-020 has the same hole for its own behaviours
9-11 (red's own bootstrap reds, uncapturable by definition).

Backfilling the logs now would be a lie about when the failure was observed,
and `bisellium red` refuses it by design. The reds are not manufactured. The
gap is recorded here, in the evidence the close rests on, and belongs in the
retro as a cascade-orchestration finding: the "land X on master first"
dependency between two opera in one cascade has no mechanism behind it.

Passed on the work, with that gap named.
